{{also|hvila}}
==Faroese==

===Etymology===
From {{der|fo|non|hvíla}}, akin to {{cog|got|𐍈𐌴𐌹𐌻𐌰𐌽||to pause, cease}}, from {{cog|got|𐍈𐌴𐌹𐌻𐌰||hour}}, akin to {{cog|goh|hwila||a while}} (or {{m|goh|wila}} or {{m|goh|hwil}}), compare {{cog|de|Weile}}.

===Noun===
{{fo-noun|f|hvílu|hvílur}}

# {{lb|fo|poetic}} [[bed]]
# {{l|en|rest}}

====Declension====
{{fo-decl-noun-f1|hvíl}}

===Verb===
{{fo-verb|hvíldi|hvílt}}

# to [[rest]]

====Conjugation====
{{fo-conj-1|hvíl}}

----

==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{der|is|non|hvíla}}, akin to {{cog|got|𐍈𐌴𐌹𐌻𐌰𐌽||to pause, cease}}, from {{cog|got|𐍈𐌴𐌹𐌻𐌰||hour}}, akin to {{cog|goh|hwila||a while}} (or {{m|goh|wila}} or {{m|goh|hwil}}), compare {{cog|de|Weile}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈkʰviːla/}}
* {{rhymes|is|iːla|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|f|hvílu|hvílan}}

# {{lb|is|dated}} [[bed]]

====Declension====
{{is-decl-noun-f-w1|hv|í|l}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb|hvíldi|hvílt}}

# {{lb|is|with accusative}} to [[rest]], especially resting or sleeping in a bed
#: {{ux|is|Hér '''hvílir''' Jóhannes.|Here '''rests''' Johannes.}}
# {{lb|is|with accusative}} to [[lie]], to [[sleep]]

====Conjugation====
{{is-conj-w2|hv|í|l}}

====Derived terms====
{{der-top}}
* {{l|is|hvíla hjá}}
* {{l|is|hvíla sig}}
{{der-mid}}
* {{l|is|hvílast}}
* {{l|is|hvíla þungt á}}
{{der-bottom}}

====See also====
* Danish: [[her hviler]]

